abstract="The input/output memory management unit (IOMMU) was recently introduced into mainstream computer architecture when both Intel and AMD added IOMMUs to their chip-sets. An IOMMU provides memory protection from I/O devices by enabling system software to control which areas of physical memory an I/O device may access. However, this protection incurs additional direct memory access (DMA) overhead due to the required address resolution and validation.",
